      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. can u add a bit more legal weight to it? like mention that under german rental law i might have grounds for a rent reduction (Mietminderung) if the heating isn't fixed quickly. i want them to take it seriously so they dont just ignore me for weeks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You want to add a legal edge, so we can make the letter sound less like a polite request and more like a formal notice. I can certainly incorporate a reference to your rights under German tenancy law regarding heating failures.\n\nHere is the revised version, which adds a more serious tone while remaining professional.\n\n***\n\n**Subject: FORMAL URGENT NOTICE: Heating Failure in Apartment [Your Apartment Number] – Demand for Immediate Repair**\n\nDear [Hausverwaltung Name or Specific Contact Person],\n\nI am writing to formally report a significant maintenance failure in my apartment, [Your Apartment Number], located at [Your Street Address]. My living room radiator ceased functioning completely yesterday, [Date], resulting in a substantial and unacceptable drop in indoor temperature.\n\nAs the heating system is a fundamental part of the habitability of the rented property, I must insist that this repair be treated with the utmost urgency, as per the obligations under German tenancy law. Please be advised that if this essential repair is not addressed and rectified within a reasonable and short timeframe, I will be compelled to explore all my legal rights, including, but not limited to, claiming a rent reduction (*Mietminderung*) for the period the heating is non-functional.\n\nI",
      "source": "target",
